<title>UK: Hanson firm after ADRs rise in New York.</title>
<headline>Hanson firm after ADRs rise in New York.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hanson Plc were up 4p at 85-1/2p by 0950 GMT following a late jump in the company's ADRs in New York on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Americans started buying Hanson ADRs in the final 15 minutes of trade last night. They were a dog stock last year so it was a case of the dog finally having its day,&quot; one senior trader said.</p>
<p>In New York on Monday, Hanson ADRs closed at $7-3/8, up $5/8 on the day.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
